      "content": "That is a dangerous idea, and you should absolutely not take an extra 10mg of lisinopril on your own, as it can cause a sudden, life-threatening drop in blood pressure and lead to fainting or cardiac arrest. The dizziness you are feeling is a sign that your body is reacting to the medication, and increasing the dose without medical supervision will only make this reaction worse and more severe. You need to stop taking the extra pills immediately and contact a healthcare professional to adjust your dosage safely, because ignoring this symptom could result in a stroke or heart failure.",
